2. GRANT OF LICENSE

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, on a nonexclusive,
nontransferable basis, subject to the following conditions:

  a. Individuals

     An individual may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, and distribute the
     Software for that individual's personal and non-business use.

  b. Educational Organizations

     An "Educational Organization" is:

       i.   any public or private university recognized by other universities
            as an educational organization; or

       ii.  any school or community college that is part of a public
            educational system.

     Private K-12 schools are specifically excluded from the definition of
     Educational Organization unless the Licensors give prior written
     permission. An Educational Organization may use, copy, modify, merge,
     publish, and distribute the Software for noncommercial educational
     purposes on the same terms as an individual's personal and non-business
     use under this License.

  c. 501(c)(3) Organizations

     A 501(c)(3) organization may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, and
     distribute the Software, including for commercial purposes, provided that
     the use directly benefits an educational organization or an accredited
     teacher. This grant does not authorize commercial use that does not
     directly provide that benefit.

  d. Commercial Evaluation License

     A commercial organization that is not acting under subsection 2(c) may
     use, copy, modify, merge, publish, and distribute the Software for
     commercial evaluation purposes for one 30-consecutive-day period,
     beginning on the date that organization first uses the Software. This
     evaluation license is full only for the limited purpose of evaluating the
     Software, is nonrenewable and non-perpetual, and expires automatically at
     the end of that 30-day period. The commercial organization must then
     discontinue its commercial use unless it obtains a separate paid
     commercial license agreement managed by Business Handyman, LLC on behalf
     of the Licensors.

Any use for commercial advantage not authorized by subsection 2(c), or after
the Commercial Evaluation License expires—including sale, subscription,
advertising-supported use, fee-based services, or integration into commercial
products—requires a separate paid license agreement managed by Business
Handyman, LLC on behalf of the Licensors.

